<!--
Cadet Fitness Assistant - Standalone Webpage

FILES INCLUDED IN THIS SINGLE HTML FOR EASE OF DEPLOYMENT:
1) index.html (this file) - contains frontend chat UI and instructions
2) Serverless function example (Node) is included below inside a comment block. Deploy this on Vercel/Netlify (recommended) and set environment var OPENAI_API_KEY.

Deployment steps summary:
- Upload this file as index.html to a public GitHub repo and enable GitHub Pages (branch: main, /root)
- Deploy the serverless function (example provided) to Vercel/Netlify or any server that can securely store your OpenAI API key.
- Update `API_ENDPOINT` in the script below to point to your deployed serverless endpoint (e.g. https://your-deploy.vercel.app/api/chat)

IMPORTANT: Do NOT put your OpenAI API key directly into this file. Keep it on the serverless function only.

ASSISTANT SYSTEM PROMPT (already embedded in requests to the serverless endpoint):
- The assistant is a fitness helper for Cadets at the United States Military Academy (West Point).
- Always assume cadets have early wakeups, heavy academics, limited downtime, and only 2 hours/day to train (gym + running).
- Advice must fit trainings in Arvin Gym or outdoor running, prioritize ACFT/APFT, injury prevention, progressive overload, and realistic cadet schedules.
- Tone: motivational, realistic, efficient. Reference the "2-hour limit" and West Point constraints in answers.
-->

